Bootstrap: docker
From: idossha/ti-toolbox:v3.1.1

# The published release image, unchanged: the SIF runs the software the Docker app runs.
# dev/update/update_version.py stamps the tag above on every release. Build (root or --fakeroot):
#   apptainer build ti-toolbox.sif apptainer.def

%post
    # Apptainer runs as the calling user, but SimNIBS is installed under /root (700, its env 750).
    chmod -R a+rX /root

%runscript
    # No arguments opens a shell. The image's own entrypoint starts tit.server, which the desktop
    # app manages over Docker; it is not a supported way to run this SIF.
    if [ $# -eq 0 ]; then
        exec /bin/bash
    fi
    exec "$@"

%test
    # The Docker build's last check: SimNIBS 4.6.0, NumPy 2.3.5, Blender outside the SimNIBS env.
    simnibs_python /ti-toolbox/container/blueprint/verify_runtime.py

%help
    TI-Toolbox as a SIF, built from the release Docker image.

      apptainer exec --bind /data/study:/mnt/study ti-toolbox.sif \
          simnibs_python -m tit.sim /mnt/study/config.json
      apptainer run --bind /data/study:/mnt/study ti-toolbox.sif   # interactive shell

    container/blueprint/apptainer_run.sh wraps these and prints a Slurm template.
    Not validated for v3: https://idossha.github.io/TI-Toolbox/installation/hpc-apptainer/
